# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD points at
# entrypoint.ps1, which is PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * the pysnmp agent is launched in the BACKGROUND via Start-Process
#     (-WindowStyle Hidden), so python is a detached child, NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep -Seconds 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the SNMP agent is ALREADY LISTENING with the
# vulnerable 'public' RW community, so a fix must restart/reconfigure the agent
# (safe now - it is not PID 1) for the live checks to pass.
